# release: the flow of depot yardr's releases. A release bead is one version,
# titled "yardr vX.Y.Z": build tags the base, waits for the draft CI makes
# for the tag (the linux archives) and adds the darwin archives it builds,
# signed and notarized, on the Mac the group runs on; mckean signs the
# draft's checksums by hand, verify checks the signature, each linux
# archive's attestation and each darwin archive's signature, and publish
# releases the draft and files the yardr.dev sync bead. The script the exec
# group runs is contrib/release/stage; docs/install.md "Making a release"
# says how a release is cut with the yard. A failed verify asks for the
# signature again; anything else failed or questioned waits in decide for a
# person, who advances it to the stage it should retry.
backlog -> build
build -> sign on done | decide on failed | decide on question
sign -> verify on done
verify -> publish on done | sign on failed | decide on question
publish -> published on done | decide on failed | decide on question
decide -> backlog | build | sign | verify | publish
published terminal
